hubspot/src/app/functions/node_modules/

upload.log

# Scratch from an /impeccable critique run. The assessment agents write probe
# scripts beside the repo while they measure the live site; the findings land
# in .impeccable/critique/, and these do not need keeping.
#
# The probe scripts have to live at the repo root, because that is where the
# Playwright install is resolvable from — an agent running them out of a temp
# directory gets ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND. So they are named, not relocated: the
# dot-prefixed patterns below cover the throwaway .mjs files, the screenshot
# directories they write, and the measurement dumps, in both assessments.
# Two agents, two prefixes, everything they write: probe scripts, screenshot
# directories, and the measurement dumps they read back. Naming the extensions
# individually was already wrong once — the review agent's next run wrote
# .a-fn1.txt through .a-fn15.txt and none of the patterns caught them.
.critique-*/
.a-*
.b-*
.m[0-9]*.mjs
.v[0-9]*.mjs

# The live-server's own runtime state: the port it bound, and the annotation
# overlays it serves back into the page. Recreated on every run.
.impeccable/live/
